# ng content

<ng-content> is a special Angular tag used to enable content projection — i.e., inserting content from a parent component into a child component’s template.

It’s kind of like saying:

“Hey parent! Send me some HTML and I’ll display it right here.”

# content projection
Content Projection is the process where Angular lets you pass HTML content (like buttons, text, images, or even components) from the parent component into a child component using <ng-content>.

